(227271, 12933, 3942, '<td valign="top">For those who are interested in, some more information about this shot:<br/> <br/>The Location is an military training area nearby my hometown. But at the weekend it is allowed to enter at one''s own risk. We waited until the afternoon to get the sunlight from the left side. I wanted to see the light only on the storefront and on the model. The rooms behind the windows should be dark to highlight the composition with the 4 different windows. In addition the extreme sidelight causes better contrasts. The shot was taken from the roof of a small building vis-à-vis and the camera position was approximately at the level of the middle of my shot. Otherwise (by shooting bottom-up) the perspective in the vertical lines would have destroyed the balance in the composition.<br/> <br/>Thanks to all of you for giving me the missing red one too :-)!<br/></td>', 'For those who are interested in, some more information about this shot: The Location is an military training area nearby my hometown. But at the weekend it is allowed to enter at one''s own risk. We waited until the afternoon to get the sunlight from the left side. I wanted to see the light only on the storefront and on the model. The rooms behind the windows should be dark to highlight the composition with the 4 different windows. In addition the extreme sidelight causes better contrasts. The shot was taken from the roof of a small building vis-à-vis and the camera position was approximately at the level of the middle of my shot. Otherwise (by shooting bottom-up) the perspective in the vertical lines would have destroyed the balance in the composition. Thanks to all of you for giving me the missing red one too :-)!', '2003-03-03 06:35:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(227272, 13040, 2221, '<td valign="top">I was very surprised to see how the score had risen during the week. Never expected such a high score for this kind of photo. So I''m very happy, especially because many said that even they normally don''t like this kind of digitally manipulated images, they think it works well for this theme. But beware, this only encourages me to refine my skills in digital work ;)<br/> <br/>See the "Photographer''s Comments" for a description how I did the effect. It was not done with an infrared filter as some suspected, I don''t own one (yet!). The "trick" is the colour inversion.<br/> <br/>Thanks to all for your feedback. Very appreciated!<br/></td>', 'I was very surprised to see how the score had risen during the week. Never expected such a high score for this kind of photo. So I''m very happy, especially because many said that even they normally don''t like this kind of digitally manipulated images, they think it works well for this theme. But beware, this only encourages me to refine my skills in digital work ;) See the "Photographer''s Comments" for a description how I did the effect. It was not done with an infrared filter as some suspected, I don''t own one (yet!). The "trick" is the colour inversion. Thanks to all for your feedback. Very appreciated!', '2003-03-03 06:38:34.000000', NULL, 0),
