(227310, 12775, 6458, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the great comments and the great voting! I knew this was a good pic, but I was worried about getting the emotion I felt across. Evidently I succeeded! You can see the original photo <a href="//matt.mbardeen.net/diary/showpicture.php?pictureid=98" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">here</a> and the entire pier <a href="//matt.mbardeen.net/diary/showpicture.php?pictureid=95" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">here</a>. I would have liked to include a picture of it before it collapsed, but, alas.. Anyway, if you''re interested you can see one <a href="//matt.mbardeen.net/olddiary/showpicture.php?pictureid=58" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">here</a>.<br/> <br/>Oh.. for those wondered what happened: A combination of neglect and weather brought it down around christmas time.. I was able to get this shot due to a really low tide the day I was shooting. There were tons of other people out that day, but luck was on my side and I only got one of them in the shot (you need to brighten up the pic to find them though!)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-03-03 08:38:10.</i></td>', 'Thanks for all the great comments and the great voting! I knew this was a good pic, but I was worried about getting the emotion I felt across. Evidently I succeeded! You can see the original photo here and the entire pier here. I would have liked to include a picture of it before it collapsed, but, alas.. Anyway, if you''re interested you can see one here. Oh.. for those wondered what happened: A combination of neglect and weather brought it down around christmas time.. I was able to get this shot due to a really low tide the day I was shooting. There were tons of other people out that day, but luck was on my side and I only got one of them in the shot (you need to brighten up the pic to find them though!)', '2003-03-03 08:34:05.000000', '2003-03-03 08:38:10.000000', 0),
