(227406, 13040, 3087, '<td valign="top"><b>Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/> <br/><b>Initial thoughts</b> <br/>High impact with obvious emotional message.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/ Content</b> <br/>I like the composition of this image  the balance of the implosion with the leaning man and the grassy earth is strong.<br/>The stance of the man is highly emotive  he looks drained, tired, sad, despairing.<br/>The white highlights in what is otherwise a silhouette are also interesting as are the white plants.<br/> <br/><b>Background</b> <br/>If one takes the implosion as the background  I like it  great shape and the texture is kind of like paint brush strokes.<br/> <br/><b>Camera Work - Technical</b> <br/>Hard to tell.<br/> <br/><b>Digital Processing - Technical</b> <br/>I am really no expert on this style of post-processing so I dont know how to comment. Given that the image is high impact and emotive Id hazard that the processing has achieved what you intended.<br/> <br/><b>Fits The Challenge</b> <br/>Yes.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion On The Photo</b> <br/>I like it and find it interesting but wouldnt personally want it on my wall/ in my house.<br/></td>', 'Critique Club   Initial thoughts High impact with obvious emotional message. Composition/ Content I like the composition of this image  the balance of the implosion with the leaning man and the grassy earth is strong.The stance of the man is highly emotive  he looks drained, tired, sad, despairing.The white highlights in what is otherwise a silhouette are also interesting as are the white plants. Background If one takes the implosion as the background  I like it  great shape and the texture is kind of like paint brush strokes. Camera Work - Technical Hard to tell. Digital Processing - Technical I am really no expert on this style of post-processing so I dont know how to comment. Given that the image is high impact and emotive Id hazard that the processing has achieved what you intended. Fits The Challenge Yes. My Opinion On The Photo I like it and find it interesting but wouldnt personally want it on my wall/ in my house.', '2003-03-03 10:20:23.000000', NULL, 0),
